<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil raises posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil raises posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$3.00/cubic metre or C$0.48/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$189.00/cubic metre, or C$30.05/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$183.00/cubic metre, or C$29.09/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$150.00/cubic metre, or C$23.85/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$158.00/cubic metre, or C$25.12/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
